    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"self-justifying\" feels like such a desperate attempt to cope. it's just a mental trick we play on ourselves to keep the engine running. if we're just biological machines driven by survival instincts, then the drive to \"create meaning\" is just another programmed compulsion to avoid the void. isn't it more honest to just admit that there's nothing to solve? it's like we're fighting a war against physics just to keep a flame alive that doesn't actually provide any light.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
